.TH SPEED-OF-CINNAMON-ALARMS 1 "June 2026" "speed-of-cinnamon 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
speed-of-cinnamon alarms \- manage Cinnamon-local repeating alarms
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B speed-of-cinnamon alarms
.RI COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Speed of Cinnamon alarms are local repeating reminders for the Cinnamon applet.
Alarm definitions are stored in a per-user JSON file. The backend checks which
alarms are due, and the applet decides whether to show Cinnamon notifications.
No portal notification service or remote desktop service is involved.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List configured alarms and scheduler metadata.
.TP
.B add
Create a repeating alarm.
.TP
.B check
Return alarms due at the current time.
.TP
.B enable
Enable an alarm by id.
.TP
.B disable
Disable an alarm by id.
.TP
.B remove
Remove an alarm by id.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --time " HH:MM"
Alarm time in local 24-hour format. Required for
.BR add .
.TP
.BI --name " TEXT"
Human-readable alarm name.
.TP
.BI --days " DAYS"
Repeat rule. Accepted values are
.BR daily ,
.BR weekdays ,
.BR weekends ,
or comma-separated day codes such as
.BR mon,wed,fri .
.TP
.BI --urgency " LEVEL"
Notification urgency:
.BR silent ,
.BR normal ,
or
.BR critical .
Silent alarms are still marked due but do not notify.
.TP
.B --disabled
Create an alarm in the disabled state.
.TP
.B --mark
With
.BR check ,
mark due alarms so they are not returned repeatedly on every refresh.
.TP
.BI --catch-up-minutes " MINUTES"
With
.BR check ,
include alarms that became due shortly before the current check.
.TP
.B --json
Print machine-readable JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a weekday alarm:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon alarms add --time 09:00 --name "Standup" --days weekdays --json
.EE
.PP
Check and mark due alarms:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon alarms check --mark --json
.EE
.PP
Disable and remove an alarm:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon alarms disable alarm-0900 --json
speed-of-cinnamon alarms remove alarm-0900 --json
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/speed-of-cinnamon/alarms.json
Per-user alarm store.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR speed-of-cinnamon (1)
